<http://www.w3.org/2006/time#intervalDisjoint> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "If a proper interval T1 is intervalDisjoint another proper interval T2, then the beginning of T1 is after the end of T2, or the end of T1 is before the beginning of T2, i.e. the intervals do not overlap in any way, but their ordering relationship is not known."@en .
